<!--
/**
 * Copyright © Magenx. All rights reserved.
 *
 * The tool registry is the module's extension point: another module adds a tool
 * by contributing one item to the `tools` argument, and it is picked up by
 * tools/list and tools/call with all of the server's guards already applied.
 *
 * Every tool is registered as a `\Proxy`, and a contributed one should be too.
 * The object manager builds an array argument eagerly, so without them a single
 * tools/call would construct all of these tools and every repository, factory
 * and collection factory each one asks for, to use exactly one. The item's key
 * is the tool's name, which is what lets the registry file a tool without
 * waking its proxy to ask; keep the two in step, as the registration
 * conventions test requires.
 */
-->
